  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chefland's jail has NNN prison cells, all arranged in a row.\n\nAbove each prison cell is a light.\n\nEach light can be made to face either left or right (but not both).\n\nThe lights aren't very strong, and so can only light up adjacent cells. In particular,\n\n\nIf the light at index iii is facing right, it will light up cells iii and i+1i+1i+1 (the latter only if i+1≤Ni+1 \\leq Ni+1≤N).\nIf the light at index iii is facing left, it will light up cells iii and i−1i-1i−1 (the latter only if i−1≥1i-1 \\geq 1i−1≥1).\nUnfortunately, due to a lack of maintenance, not all of the lights are working.\n\nYou are given a binary string SSS of length NNN, where Si=1S_i = 1Si​=1 means the iii-th light is working, and Si=0S_i = 0Si​=0 means it's not working.\n\nIs it possible to choose the directions for all the working lights, so that every cell is lit up by at least one light?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of cells.\nThe second line contains a binary string SSS of length NNN, denoting information about which lights work.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: `Yes` if there's a way to choose directions for the lights and light up every cell, and `No` otherwise.\n\n\nEach character of the output may be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e. the strings `NO`, `No`, `nO`, and `no` will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100",
      "Si∈{0,1}S_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Si​∈{0,1}"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n5\n10011\n5\n01010\n6\n110100\n7\n0110011",
        "output": "Yes\nNo\nNo\nYes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The lights at positions 1,4,51, 4, 51,4,5 are working. Consider the following configuration:\n\nLight 111 faces right. This lights up cells 1,21, 21,2.\nLight 444 faces left. This lights up cells 3,43, 43,4.\nLight 555 faces left. This lights up cells 4,54, 54,5.\nAll cells are now lit up.\n\nTest case 222: The lights at positions 2,42, 42,4 are active.\nTo light up cell 111, the light at 222 must face left.\nTo light up cell 555, the light at 444 must face right.\nBut then this leaves position 333 unlit.\nSo, it's impossible to light up all the cells.\nTest case 333: There's no way to light up the last cell.\nTest case 444: The lights at positions 2,3,6,72, 3, 6, 72,3,6,7 are active.\nOne valid configuration is to make them face directions left, right, left, right, respectively."
      }
    ]
